### FLEARN Backlog API Test Suite
### Use REST Client extension in VS Code to run these tests

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8099
@token = YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE
@userId = YOUR_USER_UUID_HERE
@subjectId = 1
@topicId = 1

### ============================================
### 1. Health Check
### ============================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### ============================================
### 2. Create Backlog Entry (Correct Answer)
### Requires Authentication
### ============================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "subject_id": 1,
  "topic_id": 1,
  "correctness": true
}

### ============================================
### 3. Create Backlog Entry (Incorrect Answer)
### Requires Authentication
### ============================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "subject_id": 1,
  "topic_id": 2,
  "correctness": false
}

### ============================================
### 4. Create Backlog Entry Without Topic
### Requires Authentication
### ============================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "subject_id": 2,
  "correctness": true
}

### ============================================
### 5. Create Backlog Entry - Missing Required Fields
### Should return 400 error
### ============================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "correctness": true
}

### ============================================
### 6. Create Backlog Entry - Invalid Correctness Type
### Should return 400 error
### ============================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "subject_id": 1,
  "correctness": "yes"
}

### ============================================
### 7. Get All Backlog Entries for User
### Requires Authentication
### ============================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog/user/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================
### 8. Get Backlog Entries with Limit and Offset
### Requires Authentication
### ============================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog/user/{{userId}}?limit=10&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================
### 9. Get Backlog Entries Filtered by Subject
### Requires Authentication
### ============================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog/user/{{userId}}?subject_id={{subjectId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================
### 10. Get Backlog Entries Filtered by Topic
### Requires Authentication
### ============================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog/user/{{userId}}?topic_id={{topicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================
### 11. Get Only Correct Answers
### Requires Authentication
### ============================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog/user/{{userId}}?correctness=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================
### 12. Get Only Incorrect Answers
### Requires Authentication
### ============================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog/user/{{userId}}?correctness=false
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================
### 13. Get Backlog Entry by ID
### Replace 1 with actual row_id from previous responses
### ============================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================
### 14. Get Overall Statistics for User
### Requires Authentication
### ============================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog/stats/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================
### 15. Get Statistics Filtered by Subject
### Requires Authentication
### ============================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog/stats/{{userId}}?subject_id={{subjectId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================
### 16. Get Statistics Filtered by Topic
### Requires Authentication
### ============================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog/stats/{{userId}}?topic_id={{topicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================
### 17. Get Statistics with Date Range
### Requires Authentication
### ============================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog/stats/{{userId}}?start_date=2025-10-01&end_date=2025-10-27
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================
### 18. Get Statistics by Subject
### Requires Authentication
### ============================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog/stats/subject/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================
### 19. Get Statistics by Topic
### Requires Authentication
### ============================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog/stats/topic/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================
### 20. Get Statistics by Topic for Specific Subject
### Requires Authentication
### ============================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog/stats/topic/{{userId}}?subject_id={{subjectId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================
### 21. Delete Specific Backlog Entry
### Replace 1 with actual row_id
### Requires Authentication
### ============================================
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================
### 22. Delete All Backlog Entries for User
### USE WITH CAUTION - This deletes all entries
### Requires Authentication
### ============================================
# DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog/user/{{userId}}
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================
### EXAMPLE TEST FLOW
### ============================================

### Step 1: Create some test entries
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "subject_id": 1,
  "topic_id": 1,
  "correctness": true
}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "subject_id": 1,
  "topic_id": 1,
  "correctness": false
}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "user_id": "{{userId}}",
  "subject_id": 1,
  "topic_id": 2,
  "correctness": true
}

### Step 2: View all entries
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog/user/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Step 3: Check statistics
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog/stats/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Step 4: Check subject breakdown
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog/stats/subject/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Step 5: Check topic breakdown
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/backlog/stats/topic/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
